# checker.dawn: K3 of docs/mem-buffer-design.md, rule R1, the plain shape (N1).
# `with_mem` is pure only if nothing it returns can reach a buffer, so a result
# of type `I64Buf` is refused at the call. The same fixture, with the rule off,
# has to compile: that is what tells a refusal that fires from one that was
# never there.
use std/mem

pub fn leak() -> I64Buf = mem.with_mem(() => mem.new(4))
